  "transcript": "He moved the pencil along to the ninth. Westerly Harbour Pump House, Keeper's Book, 2604, 11th, third month. At three, the stepped lamps on the key white. Town lamps out half hour. Keeper, ill of a fever. His wife sat up. He said, in the morning, the roof was off. Not fault. Kiva read it twice. She was aware of Polglaze's tape going round on its spool and of the timber pond's water moving under the boards, low on the ebb. No doubt."
